The shop assistant looks at the receipt.
She sees that I bought the shirt today.
"Everything is in order," she says.
"Which size do you need?"
The yellow shirt on the counter is size M.
"I need it one size bigger, please," I answer.
"Size L is certainly better than size M."
"I will check if we still have size L," the woman says.
She smiles warmly.
She takes the small shirt from the counter.
Then she walks to the stockroom.
I wait at the customer service desk.
Hopefully they still have the shirt in the right size.
I really like the color, after all.
After a short time, the door of the stockroom opens.
The assistant comes back.
She has a yellow shirt in her hand.
